        "vid": "eab90fc5-8bb7-11f1-a6ab-bc241121aa0a"
    },
    "details": "# Problem Description:\n\nTo retrieve the previous timer value, the kernel calls\nrealtimer_gettime(), which obtains the current time for the timer\\'s\nclock. For a timer using CLOCK_TAI this can fail when no TAI offset has\nbeen configured, but the error return was not checked, so the\nuninitialized output buffer was copied to userspace.\n\n# Impact:\n\nAn unprivileged local user can obtain uninitialized kernel stack memory\nby creating a POSIX timer with CLOCK_TAI and calling timer_settime(2),\npotentially disclosing sensitive kernel data.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0365",
